# Common mistakes with the math functions: a string or datetime where a number is needed, and wrong
# argument counts.
mode: check
schema: 'orders.csv'(orderId: string, customerId: string, amount: real, qty: long, timestamp: datetime)
---- query
from 'orders.csv'
| project
    a = abs(customerId),
    b = round(amount, 1.5),
    c = floor(timestamp),
    d = ceiling(),
    e = sqrt(customerId),
    f = pow(amount),
    g = log(timestamp),
    h = log10(),
    i = exp(amount, 2)
---- expected
error[DS2006]: argument `x` of `abs` must be a number or `timespan`, found `string`
  --> query:3:13
  |
3 |     a = abs(customerId),
  |             ^^^^^^^^^^ this is `string` (column `customerId` was read from orders.csv)
  |
  = note: `abs` has these forms: `abs(x: T) -> long or real`, where T is a number; `abs(x: timespan) -> timespan`

error[DS2006]: argument `digits` of `round` must be an integer (`int` or `long`), found `real`
  --> query:4:23
  |
4 |     b = round(amount, 1.5),
  |                       ^^^ this is `real`
  |
  = help: convert it first if that is what you meant: `tolong(1.5)`
  = note: signature: `round(x: T[, digits: integer]) -> long or real`, where T is a number

error[DS2006]: argument `x` of `floor` must be a number, found `datetime`
  --> query:5:15
  |
5 |     c = floor(timestamp),
  |               ^^^^^^^^^ this is `datetime` (column `timestamp` was read from orders.csv)
  |
  = note: signature: `floor(x: T) -> long or real`, where T is a number

error[DS2002]: `ceiling` takes 1 argument, found 0
  --> query:6:9
  |
6 |     d = ceiling(),
  |         ^^^^^^^^^ missing `x`
  |
  = note: signature: `ceiling(x: T) -> long or real`, where T is a number

error[DS2006]: argument `x` of `sqrt` must be a number, found `string`
  --> query:7:14
  |
7 |     e = sqrt(customerId),
  |              ^^^^^^^^^^ this is `string` (column `customerId` was read from orders.csv)
  |
  = help: convert it first if that is what you meant: `toreal(customerId)`
  = note: signature: `sqrt(x: number) -> real`

error[DS2002]: `pow` takes 2 arguments, found 1
  --> query:8:9
  |
8 |     f = pow(amount),
  |         ^^^^^^^^^^^ missing `exponent`
  |
  = note: signature: `pow(base: number, exponent: number) -> real`

error[DS2006]: argument `x` of `log` must be a number, found `datetime`
  --> query:9:13
  |
9 |     g = log(timestamp),
  |             ^^^^^^^^^ this is `datetime` (column `timestamp` was read from orders.csv)
  |
  = note: signature: `log(x: number) -> real`

error[DS2002]: `log10` takes 1 argument, found 0
   --> query:10:9
   |
10 |     h = log10(),
   |         ^^^^^^^ missing `x`
   |
   = note: signature: `log10(x: number) -> real`

error[DS2002]: `exp` takes 1 argument, found 2
   --> query:11:21
   |
11 |     i = exp(amount, 2)
   |                     ^ this argument is not expected
   |
   = note: signature: `exp(x: number) -> real`
